253
00:19:11.067 --> 00:19:12.649
A lot of people.

254
00:19:13.027 --> 00:19:16.065
No one needs to get hurt
anymore. David.

255
00:19:28.167 --> 00:19:29.999
OVERSEER:
It's gonna be okay. Joseph.

256
00:19:31.337 --> 00:19:33.690
DR. STAPLE: (OVER SPEAKER) <i>Take them
straight to Raven Hill Memorial.</i>

257
00:19:33.714 --> 00:19:36.456
<i>The west wing
of Raven Hill Memorial.</i>

258
00:19:38.511 --> 00:19:41.094
(INDISTINCT CLAMORING
OVER RADIO)

259
00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:42.261
(RADIO STOPS)

260
00:19:45.059 --> 00:19:46.345
(GASPS)

261
00:19:50.523 --> 00:19:52.139
(DOOR BUZZING)

262
00:19:56.821 --> 00:19:57.821
OFFICER: No problem.

263
00:20:07.289 --> 00:20:08.996
(DOOR BUZZING)

264
00:20:12.545 --> 00:20:13.751
OFFICER: Keep moving.

265
00:20:15.464 --> 00:20:16.545
Keep moving.

266
00:20:17.425 --> 00:20:18.777
(AS HEINRICH)
Please. don't. Don't.

267
00:20:18.801 --> 00:20:20.087
Don't. No.
OFFICER 2: Easy.

268
00:20:20.469 --> 00:20:21.504
OFFICER 1: Hey! Hey!

269
00:20:21.595 --> 00:20:23.515
(AS HEDWIG) We're cool. we're cool.
Totally cool.

270
00:20:23.639 --> 00:20:27.132
All right? He doesn't like to be touched.
I can walk. I'll just walk.

271
00:20:27.727 --> 00:20:28.727
Keep walking.

272
00:20:35.359 --> 00:20:36.599
(DOOR CLOSES)

273
00:20:58.924 --> 00:21:02.588
My name is Dr. Ellie Staple
and I'm a psychiatrist.

274
00:21:04.722 --> 00:21:06.679
This room must look nefarious.

275
00:21:07.224 --> 00:21:10.637
The walls are equipped
with 46 high-pressured nozzles

276
00:21:10.728 --> 00:21:14.221
all connected to a 15.000-gallon
water tank outside.

277
00:21:15.024 --> 00:21:18.733
It will only be triggered if you
are threatening or trying to escape.

278
00:21:19.195 --> 00:21:20.981
This is a hypnosis light...

279
00:21:23.866 --> 00:21:24.901
(AS DENNIS) Dennis.

280
00:21:25.576 --> 00:21:27.567
My pleasure. Dennis.
Mmm-hmm.

281
00:21:28.704 --> 00:21:30.320
You are being monitored.

282
00:21:30.664 --> 00:21:33.326
If. for some reason. there's a
threatening identity in the room.

283
00:21:33.417 --> 00:21:34.907
the light will
automatically strobe

284
00:21:35.002 --> 00:21:37.369
and force a different identity
to take over.

285
00:21:37.546 --> 00:21:38.707
DENNIS:
Who was the man?

286
00:21:39.799 --> 00:21:41.710
He was as strong
as The Beast.

287
00:21:42.092 --> 00:21:44.675
The man people in this city
have been talking about.

288
00:21:45.054 --> 00:21:48.968
The only person to survive that
train wreck all those years ago.

289
00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:54.094
I saw a video of you fighting
near a fire hydrant that erupted.

290
00:21:54.355 --> 00:21:55.561
Saw you choke.

291
00:21:55.731 --> 00:21:58.644
I think you believe
water is your weakness.

292
00:21:58.734 --> 00:22:00.020
Where are you keeping him?

293
00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:01.316
(THE BEAST EXHALES)

294
00:22:07.117 --> 00:22:08.357
(ROARS)

295
00:22:08.619 --> 00:22:09.654
(GROANS)

296
00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:15.407
DR. STAPLE:
<i>Everyone is safe. David.</i>

297
00:22:16.544 --> 00:22:20.253
Maybe this will all make sense
if I explain who I am.

298
00:22:21.465 --> 00:22:25.754
I specialize in a particular
type of delusion of grandeur.

299
00:22:26.136 --> 00:22:31.097
I specialize in those individuals
who believe they are superheroes.

300
00:22:32.518 --> 00:22:36.102
I've been given three days to treat
you by whatever means necessary.

301
00:22:39.191 --> 00:22:41.523
I came here for you both.

302
00:22:42.486 --> 00:22:44.318
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

303
00:22:44.905 --> 00:22:46.441
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
ON PA)

304
00:23:08.762 --> 00:23:11.800
PIERCE: Yo. this doctor comes in
here. takes over our wing.

305
00:23:11.891 --> 00:23:14.553
tells us all new rules.
Rules of conduct.

306
00:23:15.436 --> 00:23:17.643
How to treat people
with kindness.

307
00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:18.970
(SCOFFS)

308
00:23:19.064 --> 00:23:21.647
My whole life. all I do
is take care of people.

309
00:23:21.817 --> 00:23:24.058
Come on. come on. come on.
There you go.

310
00:23:24.987 --> 00:23:28.070
We got along just fine without
her. didn't we? Me and you?

311
00:23:28.324 --> 00:23:30.440
(SIGHS HEAVILY)
(SLURPING)

312
00:23:30.534 --> 00:23:31.899
Anyway...

313
00:23:31.994 --> 00:23:33.325
(MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS)

314
00:23:33.412 --> 00:23:35.278
You won't be lonely anymore.

315
00:23:36.415 --> 00:23:38.031
You have two new friends.

316
00:23:40.169 --> 00:23:42.331
(SCHOOL BELL RINGING)

317
00:23:42.421 --> 00:23:43.911
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

318
00:23:58.729 --> 00:24:01.391
Casey. could I see you
for a second?

319
00:24:09.615 --> 00:24:11.697
<i>I received a call
from your foster family.</i>

320
00:24:12.284 --> 00:24:14.776
Apparently.
it's on the news.

321
00:24:15.579 --> 00:24:20.494
They caught the guy who abducted
you and murdered all those girls.

322
00:24:20.793 --> 00:24:22.204
They caught the bastard.

323
00:24:22.628 --> 00:24:24.585
Your foster family
is thrilled.

324
00:24:25.381 --> 00:24:28.123
I can imagine how much relief
this causes you.

325
00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:31.505
I'm sure you've been
thinking about him.

326
00:24:34.431 --> 00:24:37.719
I have been thinking
about him.

327
00:24:55.828 --> 00:24:58.741
They. uh. told me
to bring lots of options.

328
00:25:01.875 --> 00:25:03.115
KEVIN: (AS JADE)
Hey. cutie.

329
00:25:05.796 --> 00:25:07.082
Think you could help me?

330
00:25:08.007 --> 00:25:09.213
I'm Jade.

331
00:25:09.717 --> 00:25:12.800
They gave me a syringe for my
diabetes. but I dropped it.

332
00:25:12.886 --> 00:25:15.719
My hands get shaky
when I get low blood sugar.

333
00:25:16.181 --> 00:25:19.924
It's a little too close to the light.
Do you think you could pick it up for me?

334
00:25:31.155 --> 00:25:32.566
(CHUCKLES)

335
00:25:34.450 --> 00:25:35.450
Wow.

336
00:25:37.578 --> 00:25:38.784
Stand up.

337
00:25:39.121 --> 00:25:42.159
Let me get
a good look at you.

338
00:25:48.088 --> 00:25:50.500
You are so tall.

339
00:25:50.883 --> 00:25:55.047
Orwell and Barry are so angry
with me that I flipped.

340
00:25:55.137 --> 00:25:56.798
But the truth is.

341
00:25:57.806 --> 00:26:00.673
we really can do things
that you can't do.

342
00:26:01.727 --> 00:26:03.183
I don't understand.

343
00:26:03.312 --> 00:26:04.312
(GIGGLES)

344
00:26:08.942 --> 00:26:10.228
(DARYL GRUNTS)

345
00:26:13.489 --> 00:26:14.979
(KEVIN GROANING)

346
00:26:17.201 --> 00:26:18.942
(AS IAN)
Hey. Hey. hey!

347
00:26:19.912 --> 00:26:21.277
(GROANS)

348
00:26:21.955 --> 00:26:23.286
I'm Ian.

349
00:26:24.416 --> 00:26:26.657
All right? I'm Ian.

350
00:26:27.711 --> 00:26:30.624
(AS MARY) And I'm Mary Reynolds.
We're twins.

351
00:26:30.798 --> 00:26:32.380
Do you know
what would have happened

352
00:26:32.466 --> 00:26:34.707
if she'd have gotten
to that key. you gobshite?

353
00:26:34.802 --> 00:26:36.759
The Horde
would have killed ya.

354
00:26:36.970 --> 00:26:40.759
(AS IAN) What've you got?
You get a little hard-on? Daryl.

355
00:26:40.849 --> 00:26:42.431
Just calm down. okay?

356
00:26:43.811 --> 00:26:44.926
(KEVIN GROANS)

357
00:26:45.020 --> 00:26:49.730
(AS NORMA) I'm sorry for being with
the Horde. It's just... It's just...

358
00:26:50.359 --> 00:26:52.396
Oh. do you know.
I am tired of being sorry.

359
00:26:52.694 --> 00:26:54.059
You can call me Norma.

360
00:26:54.530 --> 00:26:56.817
I am sorry about
the whole lying thing.

361
00:26:56.907 --> 00:26:59.148
Though. I'm not lying.
Bro. just stop talking!

362
00:27:00.244 --> 00:27:02.155
(AS JALIN)
I was so amped!

363
00:27:02.538 --> 00:27:05.075
We almost got you. bro!
(LAUGHS)

364
00:27:05.207 --> 00:27:07.039
Trying to keep him here
with this light thing?

365
00:27:07.126 --> 00:27:08.787
That's some buttery shit.

366
00:27:08.877 --> 00:27:09.992
DARYL: Stop talking.

367
00:27:12.297 --> 00:27:14.137
(AS ANSEL) I'm not supposed
to be in the light.

368
00:27:14.466 --> 00:27:16.332
Oh. we need more time.

369
00:27:16.552 --> 00:27:18.088
Barry is speaking to Kevin.

370
00:27:18.178 --> 00:27:21.136
Trying to get him nearer the light.
Is he close enough yet?

371
00:27:23.559 --> 00:27:27.518
(AS B.T.) The only one
who can defend us is him.

372
00:27:27.896 --> 00:27:28.896
Him!

373
00:27:29.022 --> 00:27:30.183
(GROANING)

374
00:27:43.745 --> 00:27:45.736
(AS PATRICIA) Where is the
man in the rain poncho?

375
00:27:46.748 --> 00:27:48.034
Who is he?

376
00:27:50.043 --> 00:27:52.876
Is he just a regular man?
I need to know.

377
00:27:56.049 --> 00:27:58.666
All right. step away from the controls
now. little duck.

378
00:27:59.303 --> 00:28:01.670
That's fine.
Now just walk away.

379
00:28:05.559 --> 00:28:06.765
(DOOR LOCK BEEPS)

380
00:28:10.772 --> 00:28:14.436
That's it. Just tip-toe away.

381
00:28:17.529 --> 00:28:19.770
I try to come
once every week.

382
00:28:19.948 --> 00:28:23.907
Sometimes. I admit.
I have neglected a week here and there.

383
00:28:24.161 --> 00:28:27.449
He's changed over the years.

384
00:28:28.624 --> 00:28:30.285
I can tell he's given up.

385
00:28:31.877 --> 00:28:33.117
It's hard to see.

386
00:28:34.630 --> 00:28:36.462
He thinks he was a mistake.

387
00:28:37.716 --> 00:28:39.923
I'm not saying
he did good things.

388
00:28:40.177 --> 00:28:41.338
He didn't.

389
00:28:41.803 --> 00:28:44.591
Those poor people didn't
deserve to die like that.

390
00:28:46.934 --> 00:28:49.722
But he's trying to make sense
of who he is.

391
00:28:51.355 --> 00:28:52.971
Ain't we all doing that?

392
00:28:54.691 --> 00:28:56.432
Yes. ma'am. we are.

393
00:28:59.488 --> 00:29:01.650
They keep him
heavily sedated.

394
00:29:02.115 --> 00:29:04.482
This is an enormous
amount of sedation.

395
00:29:04.743 --> 00:29:06.484
He's too smart for 'em.

396
00:29:07.204 --> 00:29:08.740
When they first
brought him here.

397
00:29:08.830 --> 00:29:11.822
he memorized a blueprint
left out from an electrician

398
00:29:11.917 --> 00:29:15.911
and short-circuited the power
to the whole hospital.

399
00:29:17.798 --> 00:29:19.914
He's good
thinking through things.

400
00:29:22.427 --> 00:29:24.134
He has this notion

401
00:29:24.221 --> 00:29:27.930
that superheroes
are based on people like him.

402
00:29:28.350 --> 00:29:30.387
and that other gentleman
I read is here.

403
00:29:30.978 --> 00:29:32.218
Mr. Dunn.

404
00:29:33.021 --> 00:29:34.511
Would it surprise you to know

405
00:29:34.606 --> 00:29:37.598
there are more and more people
who have this delusion?

406
00:29:38.652 --> 00:29:41.314
It is actually
the center of my work.

407
00:29:43.031 --> 00:29:44.362
Yes. it would.

408
00:29:45.909 --> 00:29:47.274
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING
ON SPEAKERS)

409
00:29:49.788 --> 00:29:52.325
MRS. PRICE: You don't let
them get you down. Elijah.

410
00:29:54.167 --> 00:29:55.498
You hear me?

411
00:29:57.212 --> 00:29:58.828
Stay proud.

412
00:30:06.388 --> 00:30:07.753
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

413
00:30:08.181 --> 00:30:10.172
Step back against the wall.
please.

414
00:30:12.519 --> 00:30:13.519
(DOOR LOCK BEEPS)

415
00:30:32.080 --> 00:30:33.411
(DOOR BUZZING)

416
00:30:33.832 --> 00:30:35.243
(GENERATOR WHIRRING)

417
00:30:42.299 --> 00:30:43.835
(WATER BUBBLING)

418
00:30:55.812 --> 00:30:57.428
(COUGHING)

419
00:30:58.106 --> 00:30:59.312
(DOOR BUZZES)

420
00:31:00.650 --> 00:31:01.765
(DOOR OPENS)

421
00:31:07.741 --> 00:31:08.947
(GRUNTS)

422
00:31:12.871 --> 00:31:14.782
You're keeping him here
without guards?

423
00:31:15.332 --> 00:31:17.448
I have to get out of here
before he gets out.

424
00:31:17.542 --> 00:31:20.830
The individual who came
with you is contained.

425
00:31:22.547 --> 00:31:23.833
David.

426
00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:27.713
I would like you
to agree to have an MRI.

427
00:31:28.303 --> 00:31:29.759
You were the sole survivor

428
00:31:29.846 --> 00:31:32.304
of a devastating train
derailment 19 years ago.

429
00:31:32.391 --> 00:31:33.722
It is possible

430
00:31:34.267 --> 00:31:37.805
that there was damage to the frontal
lobe that you are unaware of.

431
00:31:46.154 --> 00:31:47.394
(EXHALES)

432
00:31:54.413 --> 00:31:55.778
Look at you. David.

433
00:31:55.956 --> 00:31:58.914
You believe you have barely
enough strength to stand up.

434
00:31:59.167 --> 00:32:01.579
You can't possibly explain
everything away.

435
00:32:03.588 --> 00:32:04.794
(GRUNTING)

436
00:32:07.050 --> 00:32:08.381
(PANTING)

437
00:32:08.468 --> 00:32:11.551
(AS MR. PRITCHARD)
Madam. I am Mr. Pritchard.

438
00:32:11.888 --> 00:32:13.470
I'm a professor of cinema.

439
00:32:13.557 --> 00:32:16.390
Specifically. Japanese.
1950s through the 1980s.

440
00:32:16.601 --> 00:32:19.013
And I have absolutely no idea
what I'm doing here.

441
00:32:19.563 --> 00:32:21.520
I am very much in favor
of Kevin's reemergence.

442
00:32:21.606 --> 00:32:24.849
And yet. I find myself
in a goddamn prison cell.

443
00:32:24.943 --> 00:32:26.559
And I can assure you
I am not...

444
00:32:27.237 --> 00:32:28.602
(GRUNTS)

445
00:32:28.822 --> 00:32:30.438
(PANTING)

446
00:32:30.949 --> 00:32:32.064
Okay.

447
00:32:34.077 --> 00:32:35.283
(YELPS)

448
00:32:37.289 --> 00:32:38.575
(PANTING)

449
00:32:40.667 --> 00:32:41.907
(AS FELIDA IN SPANISH)

450
00:32:52.304 --> 00:32:54.011
(GRUNTS. GROWLS)

451
00:32:54.431 --> 00:32:55.711
(AS HEDWIG IN ENGLISH)
I'm ready.

452
00:32:55.891 --> 00:32:56.972
(WHIMPERS)

453
00:32:57.225 --> 00:32:58.465
Young man. wait!

454
00:32:58.643 --> 00:32:59.724
(SHOES SQUEAKING)

455
00:33:00.937 --> 00:33:03.019
You will not be able
to get to the light.

456
00:33:04.649 --> 00:33:08.233
It is set off by distance as well
as being monitored by a camera.

457
00:33:09.279 --> 00:33:12.362
I know this seems very unfair to
you. (BLOWS RASPBERRY)

458
00:33:12.449 --> 00:33:14.406
but you are stuck
in this room.

459
00:33:15.118 --> 00:33:17.530
The guy The Beast fought.
he's right there!

460
00:33:18.622 --> 00:33:22.741
He can't beat The Beast. He doesn't
think he can beat The Beast. does he?

461
00:33:22.876 --> 00:33:23.876
Huh?

462
00:33:24.169 --> 00:33:25.169
Beast like... (GRUNTS)

463
00:33:28.298 --> 00:33:29.538
(PANTING)

464
00:33:30.342 --> 00:33:32.674
(WHISPERS) He doesn't think he
can beat The Beast. does he?

465
00:33:34.262 --> 00:33:35.423
Beast like... (GRUNTS SOFTLY)

466
00:33:36.640 --> 00:33:38.551
Your name is Hedwig. right?

467
00:33:40.227 --> 00:33:42.013
You're nine. right?

468
00:33:42.938 --> 00:33:43.938
HEDWIG: Yeah.

469
00:33:44.689 --> 00:33:45.929
Forever?

470
00:33:46.525 --> 00:33:47.686
(SIGHS)

471
00:33:49.361 --> 00:33:52.023
No matter how many
experiences you have?

472
00:33:55.742 --> 00:33:57.358
That must be so hard.

473
00:34:00.539 --> 00:34:03.327
You treat people who think they're
comic book characters or something?

474
00:34:06.419 --> 00:34:07.534
(EXHALES)

475
00:34:08.296 --> 00:34:09.296
(CHUCKLES)

476
00:34:10.382 --> 00:34:11.668
HEDWIG: I gotta go.

477
00:34:12.217 --> 00:34:14.128
Miss Patricia says
she wants the light.

478
00:34:27.148 --> 00:34:28.559
Hello. Patricia.

479
00:34:29.568 --> 00:34:30.899
I'm Dr. Staple.

480
00:34:31.069 --> 00:34:32.189
(AS PATRICIA) I've gathered.

481
00:34:33.530 --> 00:34:36.613
As I understand it.
you're kind of the high priestess.

482
00:34:37.826 --> 00:34:39.316
This cause isn't about me.

483
00:34:41.079 --> 00:34:42.990
It's about The Beast. is it?

484
00:34:43.540 --> 00:34:44.746
Where is he?

485
00:34:45.250 --> 00:34:46.331
DR. STAPLE: Who?

486
00:34:46.418 --> 00:34:47.533
The man.

487
00:34:49.462 --> 00:34:52.500
He is guarded. isn't he?
He can't get out?

488
00:34:56.386 --> 00:34:57.592
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

489
00:35:00.807 --> 00:35:02.297
(JOSEPH CHATTERING
AND SNICKERING)

490
00:35:05.478 --> 00:35:07.238
He's well-intentioned
and you would love him.

491
00:35:07.314 --> 00:35:09.476
He's a huge...
He's a big trickster.

492
00:35:12.277 --> 00:35:14.609
He's a great guy. He's got
a great sense of humor.

493
00:35:15.488 --> 00:35:17.300
DR. STAPLE: So. let me recap
what you've told me.

494
00:35:17.324 --> 00:35:18.405
Mmm-hmm.

495
00:35:18.491 --> 00:35:22.359
Your dad is not the Green Guard
or "whatever his name is."

496
00:35:22.454 --> 00:35:23.865
Your dad is a trickster.

497
00:35:24.164 --> 00:35:25.746
and that I would love him.

498
00:35:26.374 --> 00:35:29.207
He thought it would be fun
to be a do-gooder for a day.

499
00:35:29.294 --> 00:35:30.580
Pretend he was this guy.

500
00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:32.627
And with regard
to how he found the girls.

501
00:35:32.714 --> 00:35:34.204
you retold a humorous story

502
00:35:34.299 --> 00:35:37.212
where your dad thought the killer
might be in the factory area

503
00:35:37.302 --> 00:35:38.633
because his friend Lou.

