on real things

757
00:54:01.029 --> 00:54:03.111
and you are making
the picture.

758
00:54:03.615 --> 00:54:06.448
It is not coming to you
through mystical means.

759
00:54:14.418 --> 00:54:16.378
These are the clothes
that the patient next to you

760
00:54:16.462 --> 00:54:18.373
came in
with when he arrived.

761
00:54:19.173 --> 00:54:21.335
There's red clay
staining the pants.

762
00:54:21.425 --> 00:54:22.665
It's very visible.

763
00:54:27.848 --> 00:54:31.057
Is it possible that you saw
something on the news...

764
00:54:31.435 --> 00:54:34.268
Sorry. bro. <i>...Then saw an
adult acting like a child?</i>

765
00:54:34.563 --> 00:54:38.477
Someone who fit the bill
of someone with this disorder.

766
00:54:38.567 --> 00:54:41.104
Intuited. "This might be
the person I'm looking for."

767
00:54:41.653 --> 00:54:43.064
Saw the red clay.

768
00:54:43.322 --> 00:54:46.485
and thought he might be hiding
in a place with red clay?

769
00:54:48.410 --> 00:54:49.571
No.

770
00:54:50.871 --> 00:54:52.111
You're certain?

771
00:54:54.792 --> 00:54:58.660
You're creating a chain of
thoughts that never happened.

772
00:55:00.506 --> 00:55:03.339
(LAUGHING)

773
00:55:07.221 --> 00:55:09.553
(AS PATRICIA) You really
dissected him. Doctor.

774
00:55:10.057 --> 00:55:11.297
Good for you.

775
00:55:12.726 --> 00:55:15.343
DR. STAPLE: As I understand
it. there were many videos

776
00:55:15.437 --> 00:55:17.223
of world-class rock climbers

777
00:55:17.314 --> 00:55:19.521
on the computer in your office
at the zoo.

778
00:55:19.942 --> 00:55:22.183
It was kind of an obsession.

779
00:55:23.195 --> 00:55:27.610
Some of those climbers could actually
scale a literal wall. couldn't they?

780
00:55:27.908 --> 00:55:29.023
(EXHALES)

781
00:55:29.868 --> 00:55:31.358
What's your point. Doctor?

782
00:55:31.578 --> 00:55:32.989
It was
a practical observation

783
00:55:33.080 --> 00:55:36.163
that produced a practical
skill set in an alter.

784
00:55:36.500 --> 00:55:37.615
Mmm.

785
00:55:39.419 --> 00:55:41.251
Then how did he bend
the bars?

786
00:55:42.089 --> 00:55:44.000
The iron bars at the zoo?

787
00:55:44.842 --> 00:55:47.129
You did see those.
didn't you?

788
00:55:48.846 --> 00:55:50.211
That's not in our heads.

789
00:55:50.514 --> 00:55:55.429
The cages beneath the zoo were made
in 1874 when the zoo first opened.

790
00:55:55.769 --> 00:55:57.225
I was able to bend them

791
00:55:57.312 --> 00:56:00.100
by putting a wrench
between them and leaning back.

792
00:56:00.190 --> 00:56:04.104
Difficult. again.
But possible.

793
00:56:04.194 --> 00:56:05.194
No!

794
00:56:06.238 --> 00:56:07.524
What about the shotgun?

795
00:56:08.073 --> 00:56:10.314
He was shot.
Not once but twice.

796
00:56:10.409 --> 00:56:12.116
What does your sleeping mind
think of that?

797
00:56:12.202 --> 00:56:14.569
We've analyzed the shotgun
and the cartridges.

798
00:56:14.663 --> 00:56:16.074
They were very old.

799
00:56:16.498 --> 00:56:19.206
There was a lot of moisture
from the boiler room

800
00:56:19.293 --> 00:56:21.500
down in the locker area
where they were kept.

801
00:56:21.879 --> 00:56:24.416
The cartridges were
possibly compromised.

802
00:56:24.715 --> 00:56:27.958
And some of the pellets
hit the inside of the bars.

803
00:56:28.051 --> 00:56:29.416
(CHUCKLES)

804
00:56:30.512 --> 00:56:32.253
It is at least possible

805
00:56:32.347 --> 00:56:35.089
that there is a practical
explanation for this.

806
00:56:36.768 --> 00:56:38.099
Mmm-mmm.

807
00:56:40.814 --> 00:56:43.772
What if I suggested
something upsetting. Patricia?

808
00:56:46.278 --> 00:56:50.021
Like The Beast isn't
as powerful as you think.

809
00:56:50.782 --> 00:56:54.025
He's not much more powerful
than a strong man.

810
00:56:55.287 --> 00:56:58.700
The facts you are basing
your belief in are wrong.

811
00:57:01.752 --> 00:57:05.837
If superheroes exist.
why are there only three of you?

812
00:57:13.972 --> 00:57:15.929
CASEY: <i>When was
the first comic book written?</i>

813
00:57:16.266 --> 00:57:20.555
The first reprints of newspaper
strips in tabloid size

814
00:57:20.646 --> 00:57:22.262
happened in 1929.

815
00:57:22.731 --> 00:57:26.895
And then. in 1938.
the apotheosis happened.

816
00:57:27.402 --> 00:57:29.609
<i>Action Comics Number One</i>
launched

817
00:57:29.738 --> 00:57:32.480
with the man in the cape and
the blue tights on the cover.

818
00:57:33.075 --> 00:57:34.156
Boo-yah!

819
00:57:34.242 --> 00:57:35.448
(LAUGHS) Here we are.

820
00:57:35.661 --> 00:57:37.151
(POP MUSIC PLAYING
ON SPEAKERS)

821
00:57:43.126 --> 00:57:44.126
Thank you.

822
00:57:50.050 --> 00:57:51.506
What are you doing
back there?

823
00:57:52.719 --> 00:57:54.835
You're not one of those
Hello Kitty pervs?

824
00:57:55.555 --> 00:57:57.421
JOSEPH: I'm just looking
for something.

825
00:57:59.476 --> 00:58:01.387
Prove to someone
I'm not crazy.

826
00:58:02.229 --> 00:58:03.264
I'm leaving.

827
00:58:42.019 --> 00:58:43.680
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

828
00:59:12.716 --> 00:59:14.332
Oh. my God!

829
00:59:15.093 --> 00:59:16.333
(GASPS)

830
01:00:11.108 --> 01:00:12.644
GIRL: Catch!
BOY 1: You're it!

831
01:00:15.529 --> 01:00:17.566
I'm it. You're it!
BOY 2: Oh. no!

832
01:00:20.867 --> 01:00:21.948
(CASEY CHUCKLES)

833
01:00:22.035 --> 01:00:23.035
You're it!

834
01:00:24.079 --> 01:00:25.240
Let's play hot potato. guys!

835
01:00:25.455 --> 01:00:26.741
GIRL: Let's play hot potato!

836
01:00:28.125 --> 01:00:31.163
KIDS: (SINGING) <i>Hot
potato Hot potato</i>

837
01:00:31.253 --> 01:00:33.915
<i>Hot potato
Hot potato</i>

838
01:00:34.047 --> 01:00:37.585
<i>Hot potato. hot potato.
hot potato Hot potato. hot potato. hot</i>

839
01:00:37.843 --> 01:00:38.945
BOY 1: You're out.
GIRL: You're out.

840
01:00:38.969 --> 01:00:39.969
BOY 2: Come on. ready?

841
01:00:40.137 --> 01:00:41.343
BOY 1: <i>No!</i>
GIRL: <i>No!</i>

842
01:00:43.974 --> 01:00:47.592
KIDS: (SINGING) <i>Hot
potato Hot potato</i>

843
01:00:47.811 --> 01:00:50.724
<i>Hot potato
Hot potato</i>

844
01:00:51.022 --> 01:00:52.604
<i>Hot potato. hot potato. hot</i>

845
01:00:53.066 --> 01:00:55.307
I'm just asking you to bring
in a package if you see one

846
01:00:55.402 --> 01:00:57.734
instead of stepping over it
to come in the house.

847
01:01:00.490 --> 01:01:01.696
(DOOR SLAMS)

848
01:01:07.414 --> 01:01:08.654
Hello?

849
01:01:25.473 --> 01:01:26.929
(DOOR LOCK BEEPS)
(DOOR BUZZES)

850
01:01:51.208 --> 01:01:53.996
If. by mistake. I drop

851
01:01:55.128 --> 01:01:58.371
this heavy flashlight
on your paper legs

852
01:02:01.509 --> 01:02:03.375
no one would come check on you
for some time.

853
01:02:03.470 --> 01:02:05.552
Not until Daryl gets here
for his shift.

854
01:02:08.516 --> 01:02:10.632
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

855
01:02:13.688 --> 01:02:15.554
Have you been getting
out of your room. Elijah?

856
01:02:32.249 --> 01:02:33.410
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

857
01:02:43.969 --> 01:02:45.801
I must be losing my mind.

858
01:03:03.530 --> 01:03:04.565
(ENGINE BACKFIRES)

859
01:03:07.367 --> 01:03:09.233
(WHEELCHAIR CREAKS)

860
01:03:14.082 --> 01:03:15.762
PIERCE: Night. Joe.
JOE: Have a good night.

861
01:03:21.339 --> 01:03:23.125
PIERCE: Daryl.
Hey. my man.

862
01:03:24.301 --> 01:03:25.757
You almost made it.

863
01:03:25.844 --> 01:03:27.505
(CHUCKLES) I think
your watch is fast.

864
01:03:29.097 --> 01:03:31.008
Joe. my man!
How's it going?

865
01:03:31.099 --> 01:03:32.326
What's going on?
What's happening?

866
01:03:32.350 --> 01:03:34.328
Looking tired. man.
You still taking that multi-vitamin?

867
01:03:34.352 --> 01:03:35.433
Not like I should.

868
01:03:35.520 --> 01:03:37.386
Yeah. but listen.
you gotta take the D.

869
01:03:37.605 --> 01:03:38.686
If you don't take
Vitamin D.

870
01:03:38.773 --> 01:03:40.543
none of that stuff's going
to absorb into your body.

871
01:03:40.567 --> 01:03:41.648
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

872
01:04:56.351 --> 01:04:59.013
(WHISPERS)
Clarence Wendell Crumb.

873
01:05:13.159 --> 01:05:14.159
(GASPS)

874
01:05:16.371 --> 01:05:17.657
(CHUCKLES)

875
01:05:19.749 --> 01:05:21.615
Take a little bit of
grape seed extract

876
01:05:21.709 --> 01:05:22.770
and it'll keep it all
in there.

877
01:05:22.794 --> 01:05:24.313
You'll absorb it
into your body faster.

878
01:05:24.337 --> 01:05:26.057
Let me ask you.
how much water you drinking?

879
01:05:26.089 --> 01:05:28.831
Not enough.
Yeah. I know.

880
01:05:46.317 --> 01:05:47.773
(DOOR LOCK BEEPS)
(DOOR BUZZES)

881
01:05:51.823 --> 01:05:53.564
(WHEELS SQUEAKING)

882
01:05:55.952 --> 01:05:57.192
(AS PATRICIA) How?

883
01:05:57.287 --> 01:06:00.871
How did you get here
without anyone seeing?

884
01:06:01.916 --> 01:06:03.873
The sound of
a car backfiring occurs

885
01:06:03.960 --> 01:06:07.169
when unburned fuel vapor is
ignited by a very hot muffler

886
01:06:07.255 --> 01:06:08.996
upon the car
being turned off.

887
01:06:09.466 --> 01:06:11.127
Daryl. who takes over
at 11:00 p.m..

888
01:06:11.217 --> 01:06:13.379
suffers from this particular
vehicular malady.

889
01:06:14.387 --> 01:06:16.219
It happened
seven minutes ago.

890
01:06:16.306 --> 01:06:18.547
Couple that with the fact
that I've overheard complaints

891
01:06:18.641 --> 01:06:20.928
about how long it takes him
to get to his desk.

892
01:06:21.019 --> 01:06:22.851
He's a bit of a talker.
you see.

893
01:06:23.062 --> 01:06:24.782
I estimate I have
two to three minutes left.

894
01:06:26.566 --> 01:06:29.274
Someone has been pretending.

895
01:06:29.486 --> 01:06:30.692
Pilfered the aspirin bottle.

896
01:06:32.155 --> 01:06:35.193
Replaced the original dose of medicine
with the same amount of aspirin.

897
01:06:35.283 --> 01:06:38.116
Did sleight of hand with the
pills given to me to take daily.

898
01:06:39.245 --> 01:06:40.861
What do you want?

899
01:06:41.414 --> 01:06:42.575
Ma'am.

900
01:06:43.458 --> 01:06:48.669
I'm here to see if the tales of
the extraordinary being are real.

901
01:06:48.755 --> 01:06:50.541
The half-man. half-creature.

902
01:06:50.715 --> 01:06:51.750
Patricia.

903
01:06:52.383 --> 01:06:54.090
But I appreciate
your manners.

904
01:06:57.805 --> 01:06:59.341
I don't know anymore.

905
01:06:59.891 --> 01:07:01.677
I'm a comic book expert.
Patricia.

906
01:07:02.101 --> 01:07:04.593
I believe comic books are a
continuation of documentation

907
01:07:04.687 --> 01:07:08.555
that has gone on for centuries
of what humans are capable of.

908
01:07:08.650 --> 01:07:12.644
That they are what someone.
somewhere. saw or felt.

909
01:07:13.988 --> 01:07:17.947
Are you aware that spandex.
the underwear on the outside. and boots

910
01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:20.867
come from strongmen
in the circus in the 1930s?

911
01:07:20.954 --> 01:07:21.989
No.

912
01:07:22.080 --> 01:07:25.072
The freak show men who could do
incredible feats of strength.

913
01:07:25.583 --> 01:07:29.326
I urge you to look past the
capes and monologuing villains.

914
01:07:29.504 --> 01:07:30.869
Are you with me?

915
01:07:32.048 --> 01:07:33.163
Yes.

916
01:07:33.341 --> 01:07:35.298
I only have a minute left.

917
01:07:35.468 --> 01:07:37.459
I believe The Beast
may be part of this.

918
01:07:37.554 --> 01:07:40.387
There are references
to man/animal characters.

919
01:07:40.473 --> 01:07:43.807
The dual character.
The man who has abilities like animals.

920
01:07:43.977 --> 01:07:47.095
I'd like to meet The Beast.
see if he's real.

921
01:07:47.689 --> 01:07:52.855
If he is. then I'll get us all
out of here tomorrow night.

922
01:07:54.153 --> 01:07:55.359
(SNIFFLING)

923
01:07:56.906 --> 01:07:58.817
What's upsetting you.
Patricia?

924
01:07:59.909 --> 01:08:02.367
What if he can't do
these extraordinary things?

925
01:08:05.623 --> 01:08:07.864
What if he is just unwell?

926
01:08:09.127 --> 01:08:10.538
Like you.

927
01:08:12.505 --> 01:08:17.341
Everything extraordinary
can be explained away

928
01:08:17.510 --> 01:08:20.172
and yet it is true.

929
01:08:21.347 --> 01:08:23.384
I think deep down
you know this.

930
01:08:24.100 --> 01:08:27.513
Everything we will see and do
will have a basis in science.

931
01:08:27.729 --> 01:08:29.766
But it will have limits.

932
01:08:29.856 --> 01:08:32.518
This is the real world.
not a cartoon.

933
01:08:33.026 --> 01:08:37.520
And yet. some of us
don't die from bullets.

934
01:08:37.697 --> 01:08:41.816
Some of us
can still bend steel.

935
01:08:42.035 --> 01:08:45.824
That is not a fantasy.

936
01:08:46.164 --> 01:08:47.325
Hmm.

937
01:08:48.916 --> 01:08:51.533
If you really think
you can get us all out.

938
01:08:52.211 --> 01:08:54.327
then you may meet The Beast.

939
01:08:55.298 --> 01:08:59.007
But for your sake.
I hope he likes you.

940
01:09:01.012 --> 01:09:02.423
Tomorrow night.

941
01:09:03.514 --> 01:09:06.302
Call a board meeting
or whatever.

942
01:09:12.857 --> 01:09:14.643
What do we call you. sir?

943
01:09:17.737 --> 01:09:19.148
First name. Mister.

944
01:09:19.947 --> 01:09:22.188
Last name. Glass.

945
01:09:29.290 --> 01:09:31.247
(DOOR LOCK BEEPS)
(DOOR OPENS)

946
01:09:32.001 --> 01:09:33.491
(MOANS) What's going on?

947
01:09:33.586 --> 01:09:35.648
Be careful. Not too much
pressure when restraining him.

948
01:09:35.672 --> 01:09:36.878
Dr. Staple.
what are you doing?

949
01:09:36.964 --> 01:09:38.125
It's a sedative.
What?

950
01:09:38.257 --> 01:09:39.588
I'm sorry to do this. Elijah.
Ow!

951
01:09:39.676 --> 01:09:41.676
We saw footage of you
leaving your room last night.

952
01:09:41.761 --> 01:09:43.361
It seems you have been duping us.
No! No.

953
01:09:43.429 --> 01:09:45.074
I've moved up the procedure
to this morning.

954
01:09:45.098 --> 01:09:46.133
Wait. I have...

955
01:10:03.658 --> 01:10:05.865
DR. STAPLE: Thank you
for being careful. everyone.

956
01:10:06.536 --> 01:10:07.901
Good luck. Elijah.

957
01:10:09.872 --> 01:10:13.331
DR. STAPLE: Nothing essential is
going to change about who you are.

958
01:10:13.960 --> 01:10:15.826
I promise. my friend.

959
01:10:22.802 --> 01:10:24.384
(SWITCH CLICKS)

960
01:10:25.638 --> 01:10:27.128
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

961
01:10:31.769 --> 01:10:33.680
(CHATTER AND LAUGHTER)

962
01:10:33.771 --> 01:10:35.353
(MAN SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY
ON PA)

963
01:10:50.747 --> 01:10:51.828
Whoo!

964
01:10:52.832 --> 01:10:53.947
(LAUGHS)

965
01:10:55.042 --> 01:10:56.498
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

966
01:10:58.379 --> 01:10:59.414
Elijah!

967
01:11:01.549 --> 01:11:02.549
Whoo!

968
01:11:02.633 --> 01:11:04.965
MAN: (ON PA)
<i>So. let's all scream!</i>

969
01:11:05.052 --> 01:11:06.668
(RIDERS WHOOPING
AND SCREAMING)

970
01:11:19.901 --> 01:11:21.483
(SOBS) Elijah!

971
01:11:21.778 --> 01:11:24.395
CONDUCTOR: Ma'am.
get a hold of yourself.

972
01:11:25.573 --> 01:11:26.859
Mama!

973
01:11:27.116 --> 01:11:28.322
(GRUNTING)

974
01:11:31.496 --> 01:11:32.496
(BONES BREAKING)

975
01:11:32.580 --> 01:11:34.696
(SCREAMS)
MRS. PRICE: Elijah!

976
01:11:36.042 --> 01:11:37.624
Stop the ride!
Ma'am. step down.

977
01:11:37.710 --> 01:11:39.041
MRS. PRICE: Stop the ride!

978
01:11:42.924 --> 01:11:44.255
(PANTING)

979
01:12:05.154 --> 01:12:06.519
(KEYS JANGLING)

980
01:12:12.745 --> 01:12:13.745
(CAR LOCK CHIRPS)

981
01:12:18.543 --> 01:12:20.079
(BEEPS)
(DOOR BUZZES)

982
01:12:20.211 --> 01:12:21.355
(OLD-TIMEY MUSIC PLAYING
ON SPEAKERS)

983
01:12:21.379 --> 01:12:22.619
Dinner. Elijah.

984
01:12:25.258 --> 01:12:26.544
How you doing?

985
01:12:29.095 --> 01:12:30.677
You'll feel better tomorrow.

986
01:12:35.768 --> 01:12:37.224
Pictures are crooked.

987
01:12:49.907 --> 01:12:50.907
Hey.

988
01:12:52.702 --> 01:12:53.908
(GRUNTS)

989
01:12:56.330 --> 01:12:59.664
Took a bitch-ass long time
to find the right piece.

990
01:13:09.093 --> 01:13:10.629
(CHOKING)

991
01:13:19.228 --> 01:13:21.936
<i>First name. Mister.</i>

992
01:13:23.107 --> 01:13:26.190
Last name. Glass.

993
01:14:02.229 --> 01:14:03.594
(BEEPING)

994
01:14:16.661 --> 01:14:17.947
(DARYL CONTINUES CHOKING)

995
01:14:20.331 --> 01:14:22.163
You don't know
what it's like. Daryl.

996
01:14:22.458 --> 01:14:25.496
To be so different.
you don't know where you fit.

997
01:14:26.671 --> 01:14:28.412
It's an awful feeling.

998
01:14:29.256 --> 01:14:30.256
(BEEPS)

999
01:14:41.268 --> 01:14:43.028
KEVIN: (AS LUKE)
Hey there. buddy. What's up?

1000
01:14:43.104 --> 01:14:44.811
Patricia told us
you were coming.

1001
01:14:44.897 --> 01:14:47.980
My name is Luke.
and I am Team Horde all the way.

1002
01:14:48.067 --> 01:14:52.152
Yeah. I can intro you to everybody.
I ain't no bad <i>hombre</i> to know.

1003
01:14:52.238 --> 01:14:54.570
Everybody's gonna tell you
that I got a big mouth. though.

1004
01:14:54.657 --> 01:14:56.898
I spoil the end of movies.
Ain't true.

1005
01:14:56.993 --> 01:15:00.031
Everybody knows the priest dies
at the end of <i>The Exorcist.</i>

1006
01:15:00.413 --> 01:15:01.903
(KEVIN GRUNTS)

1007
01:15:01.998 --> 01:15:07.118
(AS GODDARD) The American Sublime.
Do you even know what that means?

1008
01:15:07.420 --> 01:15:08.455
No.

1009
01:15:08.546 --> 01:15:11.288
That is why this world
is a lost cause.

1010
01:15:11.382 --> 01:15:15.797
That is why The Beast is the only
thing that is pure and meaningful...

1011
01:15:15.886 --> 01:15:17.926
ELIJAH: American Sublime
refers to Western paintings

1012
01:15:17.972 --> 01:15:21.090
of landscapes and seascapes
depicting the immensity of nature.

1013
01:15:21.517 --> 01:15:25.010
The use of violent storms in the
distance was a common practice.

1014
01:15:25.688 --> 01:15:28.020
Painting's of particular
interest to me.

1015
01:15:28.190 --> 01:15:29.305
(GRUNTS)

1016
01:15:29.734 --> 01:15:30.734
(KEVIN GROANS)

1017
01:15:31.485 --> 01:15:34.728
(AS HEDWIG) Hey. Miss Patricia
says that your bones can break

1018
01:15:34.822 --> 01:15:36.049
if I. like.
(CLICKS TONGUE) tap them.

1019
01:15:36.073 --> 01:15:37.279
Is that true?

1020
01:15:37.783 --> 01:15:38.783
Yes.
(EXHALES)

1021
01:15:38.868 --> 01:15:42.702
Uh. so. what's your superpower?
Your mind?

1022
01:15:44.290 --> 01:15:45.576
(WHOOSHES)

1023
01:15:45.666 --> 01:15:46.997
What's mine?

1024
01:15:49.795 --> 01:15:51.581
You're nine forever.
right?

1025
01:15:52.965 --> 01:15:53.965
Yeah.

1026
01:15:54.800 --> 01:15:56.290
That's incredible.

1027
01:15:57.219 --> 01:16:01.213
You can see the world the
way it really is. Always.

1028
01:16:02.558 --> 01:16:04.140
Kid who can never grow old.

1029
01:16:04.810 --> 01:16:05.810
(CHUCKLES)

1030
01:16:07.521 --> 01:16:08.636
Are you ready?

1031
01:16:11.525 --> 01:16:14.563
Are you ready?

1032
01:16:15.613 --> 01:16:16.728
Yeah.

1033
01:16:19.241 --> 01:16:20.322
Whoa!

1034
01:16:23.120 --> 01:16:25.862
This place is so cool.
Mr. Glass.

1035
01:16:26.957 --> 01:16:28.948
I feel like dancing.

1036
01:16:29.794 --> 01:16:31.125
Then go ahead and dance.

1037
01:16:31.295 --> 01:16:32.956
Yeah! Check it!

1038
01:16:33.255 --> 01:16:35.292
(HUMMING)

1039
01:16:39.804 --> 01:16:40.804
Yeah.

1040
01:16:48.729 --> 01:16:50.185
Oh. man.

1041
01:16:59.782 --> 01:17:01.364
(KEVIN GRUNTING)

1042
01:17:02.409 --> 01:17:03.865
(GROANING)

1043
01:17:37.695 --> 01:17:39.311
(THE BEAST GROWLING)

1044
01:17:40.823 --> 01:17:43.656
ELIJAH:
They've been lying to us all.

1045
01:17:44.451 --> 01:17:47.910
(AS THE BEAST)
You believe?

1046
01:17:49.623 --> 01:17:50.909
Yes. I do.

1047
01:17:53.627 --> 01:17:56.540
It's what I've believed
my whole life.

1048
01:18:00.092 --> 01:18:03.505
They are losing faith.

1049
01:18:03.971 --> 01:18:09.307
My Horde is losing faith!

1050
01:18:09.727 --> 01:18:11.092
In comics.

1051
01:18:12.479 --> 01:18:16.393
you would go to a public
place. where all could see you.

1052
01:18:17.026 --> 01:18:21.111
A place celebrating man's
pedestrian achievements.

1053
01:18:22.948 --> 01:18:25.110
But you need David

1054
01:18:26.202 --> 01:18:27.283
to convince them.

1055
01:18:28.078 --> 01:18:31.571
You should fight him
in front of the world.

1056
01:18:34.418 --> 01:18:38.582
The tallest building in
this city is opening today.

1057
01:18:39.840 --> 01:18:44.050
All the cameras in the
world will record you.

1058
01:18:45.429 --> 01:18:47.261
You can convince the Horde

1059
01:18:47.348 --> 01:18:50.511
and the world
at the same time.

1060
01:18:51.602 --> 01:18:53.343
we exist.

1061
01:18:53.520 --> 01:18:55.682
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1062
01:18:58.234 --> 01:19:04.276
Why are you in this chair.
child?

1063
01:19:05.032 --> 01:19:07.945
My bones break easily.

1064
01:19:08.535 --> 01:19:09.991
I was born this way.

1065
01:19:10.871 --> 01:19:13.283
I've had 94 breaks
in my life.

1066
01:19:15.042 --> 01:19:16.783
I've known only pain.

1067
01:19:17.378 --> 01:19:19.039
Rejoice.

1068
01:19:20.798 --> 01:19:26.089
You have suffered
and are now pure.

1069
01:19:27.304 --> 01:19:31.423
I assume you were sent here
to be an avenging angel.

1070
01:19:33.519 --> 01:19:36.432
How much do you want
to avenge us?

1071
01:19:44.697 --> 01:19:46.779
(YELLING)

1072
01:19:52.496 --> 01:19:57.286
Well. that sounds like
the bad guys teaming up.

1073
01:20:02.047 --> 01:20:03.727
ELIJAH: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>How you doing. David?</i>

1074
01:20:04.466 --> 01:20:06.252
<i>I always thought of us
as friends.</i>

1075
01:20:07.052 --> 01:20:08.463
Elijah?

1076
01:20:09.513 --> 01:20:12.050
ELIJAH: <i>You shouldn't be
hiding in the shadows. David.</i>

1077
01:20:12.349 --> 01:20:13.510
You're able to hide

1078
01:20:13.684 --> 01:20:16.392
because people who steal cars
and mug people in alleys

1079
01:20:16.562 --> 01:20:18.678
don't need
your full potential.

1080
01:20:18.772 --> 01:20:20.612
You're only using
one percent of your abilities

1081
01:20:20.691 --> 01:20:22.056
with these petty criminals.

1082
01:20:23.444 --> 01:20:25.981
Maybe there's nothing
to hide. Elijah.

1083
01:20:26.155 --> 01:20:30.865
<i>I have found someone who will require
your full potential to come out.</i>

1084
01:20:31.035 --> 01:20:33.026
<i>A superhuman serial killer.</i>

1085
01:20:33.579 --> 01:20:35.035
Don't do this.

1086
01:20:35.914 --> 01:20:36.949
(SIGHS)

1087
01:20:37.041 --> 01:20:39.453
How can we be
the only ones?

1088
01:20:39.626 --> 01:20:42.038
<i>Maybe we believed something
that isn't even true.</i>

1089
01:20:42.713 --> 01:20:44.044
(SIGHS)

1090
01:20:44.131 --> 01:20:48.250
We are going to the tallest
building in the city.

1091
01:20:48.344 --> 01:20:50.756
The Horde is going to be
revealed there.

1092
01:20:51.013 --> 01:20:52.344
There are three floors

1093
01:20:52.431 --> 01:20:54.513
that house a chemical company
in that building.

1094
01:20:54.683 --> 01:20:58.517
I am going to blow up that building
using their chemicals. David.

1095
01:20:58.687 --> 01:21:01.270
<i>You might want to
try and stop us.</i>

1096
01:21:02.358 --> 01:21:04.941
<i>Today is
your coming-out party.</i>

1097
01:21:05.027 --> 01:21:07.018
<i>At least you know
what to wear.</i>

1098
01:21:07.988 --> 01:21:09.069
(BEEPING)

1099
01:21:09.156 --> 01:21:11.238
(AIR HISSING)

1100
01:21:12.117 --> 01:21:13.278
(BUTTON CLICKS)

1101
01:21:14.578 --> 01:21:17.320
I've turned off the water
hoses in your room. David.

1102
01:21:17.831 --> 01:21:20.072
There's only the door left.
Elijah.

1103
01:21:20.167 --> 01:21:21.453
It's metal.

1104
01:21:21.710 --> 01:21:24.498
But you can't get through it.
because people's bones

1105
01:21:24.588 --> 01:21:28.582
<i>break against metal.
and you're nothing special.</i>

1106
01:21:29.676 --> 01:21:33.294
A lot of people
are going to die. Overseer.

1107
01:21:34.014 --> 01:21:38.508
if you don't get through
that door.

1108
01:21:38.602 --> 01:21:39.933
(SWITCH CLICKS)

1109
01:21:42.314 --> 01:21:43.520
(SIGHS)

1110
01:21:45.109 --> 01:21:46.190
Hi.
(DOOR BUZZES)

1111
01:22:00.499 --> 01:22:02.285
(FLIES BUZZING)

1112
01:22:08.966 --> 01:22:10.331
I'm here.

1113
01:22:22.062 --> 01:22:23.097
(BUTTON CLICKS)

1114
01:22:28.110 --> 01:22:29.145
(SWITCH CLICKS)

1115
01:22:29.236 --> 01:22:30.442
Daryl?

1116
01:22:31.363 --> 01:22:33.445
(WHEELS SQUEAKING IN DISTANCE)

1117
01:22:46.712 --> 01:22:48.373
(SQUEAKING CONTINUES)

1118
01:23:03.020 --> 01:23:05.227
(SQUEAKING CONTINUES)

1119
01:23:27.377 --> 01:23:29.243
This is where
they would paint you

1120
01:23:29.421 --> 01:23:33.961
with big eyes and bubbles of
confusion above your head.

1121
01:23:40.390 --> 01:23:41.596
(SOFT THUD)

1122
01:23:42.809 --> 01:23:44.015
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1123
01:23:44.102 --> 01:23:48.141
(AS THE BEAST)
You hurt him?

1124
01:23:48.690 --> 01:23:50.146
What are you doing?

1125
01:23:50.901 --> 01:23:55.646
You should kneel before him.

1126
01:23:55.822 --> 01:23:58.564
He is the broken.

1127
01:23:58.742 --> 01:24:00.858
PIERCE: Step away from me.
(GRUNTING)

1128
01:24:01.453 --> 01:24:03.694
Get back in your room!
Both of you!

1129
01:24:03.789 --> 01:24:04.995
(GRUNTS)

1130
01:24:05.082 --> 01:24:06.243
(BONES CRUNCHING)
(GASPS)

1131
01:24:06.333 --> 01:24:07.949
(SCREAMING)

1132
01:24:08.418 --> 01:24:10.375
(THE BEAST GRUNTING)
(PIERCE GASPING)

1133
01:24:12.881 --> 01:24:14.087
(SNARLING)

1134
01:24:18.303 --> 01:24:20.089
You're fighting
for the broken.

1135
01:24:21.598 --> 01:24:23.214
You found your purpose.

1136
01:24:23.308 --> 01:24:25.800
(THE BEAST GRUNTING)
(PIERCE GASPING)

1137
01:24:27.187 --> 01:24:28.677
(BONES CRUNCH)

1138
01:24:28.897 --> 01:24:30.137
(GASPS)

1139
01:24:31.316 --> 01:24:32.647
(PIERCE GRUNTS)

1140
01:24:32.901 --> 01:24:34.858
(THE BEAST BREATHING HEAVILY)

1141
01:24:35.988 --> 01:24:37.274
(THE BEAST GRUNTING)

1142
01:24:37.990 --> 01:24:39.321
(BONES CRUNCH)

1143
01:24:40.659 --> 01:24:42.024
(THE BEAST GRUNTS)
(BODY THUDS)

1144
01:24:44.913 --> 01:24:46.199
(SIGHS)

1145
01:24:46.707 --> 01:24:48.698
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1146
01:24:48.792 --> 01:24:50.533
(GRUNTING)

1147
01:24:55.090 --> 01:24:59.004
One of the Horde may need to walk
us out of here. if that's okay...

1148
01:25:00.262 --> 01:25:02.253
Partner.

1149
01:25:02.389 --> 01:25:04.676
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1150
01:25:06.018 --> 01:25:07.224
(GRUNTS)

1151
01:25:07.769 --> 01:25:09.055
(SIGHS)

1152
01:25:17.279 --> 01:25:18.279
(YELLS)

1153
01:25:39.926 --> 01:25:41.257
(YELLS AND GRUNTS)

1154
01:25:45.307 --> 01:25:47.173
(BEEPS)
(DOOR BUZZES)

1155
01:26:09.748 --> 01:26:11.580
ELIJAH: Go through
the basement.

1156
01:26:12.793 --> 01:26:13.999
(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)

1157
01:26:22.511 --> 01:26:23.546
(GRUNTS)

1158
01:28:06.990 --> 01:28:08.270
DR. STAPLE:
Listen to me. Joseph.

1159
01:28:08.325 --> 01:28:10.191
Your father is making
great progress.

1160
01:28:10.285 --> 01:28:12.242
I'm very hopeful for him.

1161
01:28:12.954 --> 01:28:16.197
Did you know
the first Superman

1162
01:28:17.083 --> 01:28:18.699
couldn't even fly?

1163
01:28:20.128 --> 01:28:22.870
And Metropolis is actually
New York City.

1164
01:28:22.964 --> 01:28:25.956
And what about all the
coincidences in what I was reading?

1165
01:28:26.051 --> 01:28:28.463
DR. STAPLE: Comic books
are an obsession.

1166
01:28:30.263 --> 01:28:32.971
Have you ever been
to a comic book convention?

1167
01:28:34.309 --> 01:28:36.721
They sell
teen TV shows there.

1168
01:28:37.395 --> 01:28:39.102
They are selling things.

1169
01:28:40.398 --> 01:28:44.858
Your friends and family members
have lost their perspective.

1170
01:28:47.489 --> 01:28:50.732
Your dad is trying
to fight her abductor.

1171
01:28:51.243 --> 01:28:53.905
Your son is trying
to best his dad.

1172
01:28:55.205 --> 01:28:58.618
He's the anarchist. he's the
brains. he's the reluctant hero.

1173
01:28:58.708 --> 01:29:01.917
This all sounds
very familiar. doesn't it?

1174
01:29:03.004 --> 01:29:05.917
Comic books
are not valid history.

1175
01:29:06.216 --> 01:29:07.877
(COMPUTER BEEPING)

1176
01:29:16.101 --> 01:29:17.842
GUARD: Hey.
what wing are you with?

1177
01:29:20.105 --> 01:29:22.166
(AS PATRICIA) Uh. The Beast
is saying that he'd like you

1178
01:29:22.190 --> 01:29:24.022
to roll forward
when they come.

1179
01:29:28.196 --> 01:29:29.436
I believe.

1180
01:29:30.532 --> 01:29:32.148
I believe.

1181
01:29:35.078 --> 01:29:36.318
I believe.

1182
01:29:42.335 --> 01:29:43.450
I believe.

1183
01:29:44.963 --> 01:29:46.203
(STRAINS)

1184
01:29:46.298 --> 01:29:47.298
(GROANS)

1185
01:29:49.301 --> 01:29:51.167
(THE BEAST BREATHING HEAVILY)

1186
01:29:54.848 --> 01:29:56.805
(ALL GRUNTING)

1187
01:30:12.032 --> 01:30:13.067
(BEEPS)
(DOOR BUZZES)

1188
01:30:32.761 --> 01:30:34.217
(INAUDIBLE)

1189
01:30:34.930 --> 01:30:36.045
(REMOTE CLICKS)

1190
01:30:36.139 --> 01:30:39.882
<i>The new Osaka building opens
today with much fanfare.</i>

1191
01:30:39.976 --> 01:30:42.559
<i>Thousands are expected to
come out for the ceremony.</i>

1192
01:30:42.646 --> 01:30:45.138
<i>Many just want to see
the spectacular architecture.</i>

1193
01:30:45.315 --> 01:30:48.774
<i>Now. this building is expected to
be the hub of the business community</i>

1194
01:30:48.860 --> 01:30:50.100
<i>creating thousands of jobs...</i>

1195
01:30:50.195 --> 01:30:51.811
We have a Code Three.

1196
01:30:52.364 --> 01:30:54.275
All patients
locked in their rooms.

1197
01:30:54.366 --> 01:30:55.948
Grounds security on alert.

1198
01:30:56.159 --> 01:30:57.219
(ON SPEAKERS) <i>The patients
are planning to go</i>

1199
01:30:57.243 --> 01:31:00.907
<i>to the public opening of the Osaka
Tower. the tallest building.</i>

1200
01:31:01.081 --> 01:31:04.244
<i>Elijah may be intending to
compromise a chemical facility there.</i>

1201
01:31:04.334 --> 01:31:07.167
<i>Please alert the Philadelphia
Police Department.</i>

1202
01:31:07.253 --> 01:31:10.120
<i>They made a mistake
going through the basement.</i>

1203
01:31:10.215 --> 01:31:11.922
<i>It gives us some time.</i>

1204
01:31:13.051 --> 01:31:16.510
MRS. PRICE: I remember something
about a classic public forum

1205
01:31:16.596 --> 01:31:19.554
where the climax of
limited editions end.

1206
01:31:19.724 --> 01:31:22.341
I think he said it was
referred to as the "showdown."

1207
01:31:23.186 --> 01:31:27.271
where all the skills are revealed
and pitted against each other.

1208
01:31:28.358 --> 01:31:29.564
And then?

1209
01:31:31.945 --> 01:31:33.481
What happens?

1210
01:31:45.291 --> 01:31:46.406
(THUDS)

1211
01:31:49.546 --> 01:31:50.752
(THUDS)
(GASPS)

1212
01:31:52.590 --> 01:31:54.206
(THE BEAST YELLING)

1213
01:31:57.303 --> 01:32:00.386
Christ! They're out here!
They're out here!

1214
01:32:05.562 --> 01:32:07.052
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

1215
01:32:15.363 --> 01:32:16.674
(ALARM BLARING)
This is Dr. Ellie Staple.

1216
01:32:16.698 --> 01:32:19.941
We will need assistance at
Raven Hill Memorial immediately.

1217
01:32:21.578 --> 01:32:24.286
(ALARM CONTINUES BLARING)

1218
01:32:39.054 --> 01:32:40.670
(BOTH SCREAMING AND GRUNTING)

1219
01:32:41.681 --> 01:32:42.681
WOMAN: No!
(WOMEN SCREAM)

1220
01:32:44.350 --> 01:32:45.966
(MUFFLED SCREAMING)

1221
01:32:47.520 --> 01:32:48.885
(PANTING)

1222
01:32:49.314 --> 01:32:51.194
(AS DENNIS) How many people
are gonna die today?

1223
01:32:51.441 --> 01:32:52.476
Huh?

1224
01:32:52.692 --> 01:32:54.148
I don't wanna do this.

1225
01:32:54.319 --> 01:32:56.981
I don't care what Patricia says.
I'm not... (STRAINING)

1226
01:32:57.614 --> 01:33:00.072
Hedwig's taking the light.

1227
01:33:00.617 --> 01:33:01.823
(AS HEDWIG) Hey. what's up?

1228
01:33:01.951 --> 01:33:02.986
(STRAINING)

1229
01:33:03.078 --> 01:33:04.118
(AS PATRICIA) Don't worry.

1230
01:33:04.204 --> 01:33:05.444
(PANTING)

1231
01:33:05.538 --> 01:33:08.530
We don't need him anyway.
There are still 10 of us.

1232
01:33:09.918 --> 01:33:11.329
(TIRES SCREECHING)

1233
01:33:15.924 --> 01:33:18.256
It appears The Beast
is not done here yet.

1234
01:33:31.064 --> 01:33:32.646
(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)

1235
01:33:36.736 --> 01:33:38.647
(THE BEAST YELLING)

1236
01:33:42.909 --> 01:33:44.866
We've got eyes on him.
Please advise.

1237
01:33:45.203 --> 01:33:47.069
(THE BEAST BREATHING HEAVILY)

1238
01:33:47.956 --> 01:33:49.196
Please advise!

1239
01:33:49.332 --> 01:33:50.618
(GRUNTING)

1240
01:33:50.750 --> 01:33:52.536
(ROARS)
(GUARDS GRUNTING)

1241
01:33:54.879 --> 01:33:55.879
(SCREAMS)

1242
01:34:01.553 --> 01:34:03.214
(DOOR OPENS)

1243
01:34:07.183 --> 01:34:10.175
The collection
of main characters.

1244
01:34:31.249 --> 01:34:33.160
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1245
01:34:33.251 --> 01:34:34.412
(GROWLS)

1246
01:34:34.502 --> 01:34:35.663
(ROARING)

1247
01:34:37.672 --> 01:34:39.788
(ALARM CONTINUES BLARING)

1248
01:34:40.425 --> 01:34:41.915
(THE BEAST ROARING)

1249
01:34:50.143 --> 01:34:51.599
(ROARING)

1250
01:34:52.770 --> 01:34:55.979
Keep patients and staff away
from the south-side windows.

1251
01:34:56.357 --> 01:34:57.893
Authorities are on their way.

1252
01:35:05.033 --> 01:35:06.615
(GRUNTING LOUDLY)

1253
01:35:13.499 --> 01:35:15.661
(WOMEN WHIMPERING)

1254
01:35:16.711 --> 01:35:18.122
(WOMEN SCREAMING)

1255
01:35:19.505 --> 01:35:21.667
Okay. I got you. (GRUNTING)

1256
01:35:23.343 --> 01:35:24.833
(BOTH WHIMPERING)

1257
01:35:28.348 --> 01:35:33.309
You will learn to kneel
before the broken.

1258
01:35:35.563 --> 01:35:38.100
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1259
01:35:41.069 --> 01:35:42.480
(YELLING)

1260
01:35:47.659 --> 01:35:48.694
(CHOKING)

1261
01:35:48.785 --> 01:35:50.401
(SIRENS WAILING)

1262
01:36:01.256 --> 01:36:02.872
(CONTINUES CHOKING)

1263
01:36:03.675 --> 01:36:05.507
(GRUNTING)

1264
01:36:16.020 --> 01:36:17.556
(OFFICERS SHOUTING
INDISTINCTLY)

1265
01:36:21.359 --> 01:36:23.475
CASEY: I need to explain.
He has DID.

1266
01:36:23.569 --> 01:36:25.464
He believes he's an animal.
OFFICER: Keep moving.

1267
01:36:25.488 --> 01:36:28.651
No. you don't understand.
All he knows is pain.

1268
01:36:28.741 --> 01:36:31.233
You're going to get hurt.
Somebody. please...

1269
01:36:31.869 --> 01:36:33.530
He has DID.

1270
01:36:33.621 --> 01:36:36.033
We can get the compassionate
people inside him to help you.

1271
01:36:36.124 --> 01:36:39.662
Stay here. ELIJAH: You're
the girl The Beast let go.

1272
01:36:44.257 --> 01:36:45.747
(YELLING)

1273
01:37:03.693 --> 01:37:05.058
(GRUNTING)

1274
01:37:05.445 --> 01:37:06.445
(SHOUTS)

1275
01:37:08.364 --> 01:37:09.479
(OFFICERS GRUNTING)

1276
01:37:09.949 --> 01:37:11.069
OVERSEER:
Stay away from him.

1277
01:37:12.327 --> 01:37:13.362
(SHOUTS)
Go!

1278
01:37:13.453 --> 01:37:14.693
(ALL GRUNTING)

1279
01:37:30.511 --> 01:37:31.797
(YELLING)

1280
01:37:34.182 --> 01:37:35.547
(GRUNTING)

1281
01:37:36.476 --> 01:37:37.682
(OFFICERS SCREAM)

1282
01:37:37.769 --> 01:37:39.305
OVERSEER: I'm just trying
to save you.

1283
01:37:44.108 --> 01:37:45.849
(GRUNTING)

1284
01:37:53.826 --> 01:37:55.112
(GASPING)

1285
01:37:55.661 --> 01:37:57.447
(GROWLING)
(WHIMPERING)

1286
01:37:58.748 --> 01:38:00.238
(GROWLING)

1287
01:38:01.084 --> 01:38:03.416
(METAL CREAKING)

1288
01:38:10.218 --> 01:38:11.379
(FLESH SQUELCHING)

1289
01:38:12.720 --> 01:38:13.926
(GRUNTS)

1290
01:38:15.848 --> 01:38:18.806
DR. STAPLE: Casey. the light
won't work out here now.

1291
01:38:19.268 --> 01:38:22.056
You have to be the one
to get Kevin to come out.

1292
01:38:22.146 --> 01:38:25.480
We need to get them inside
to safety. Do you hear me?

1293
01:38:27.318 --> 01:38:29.958
JOSEPH: (ON SPEAKERS) <i>Dad.
there are two tactical teams on the way.</i>

1294
01:38:29.987 --> 01:38:31.352
OVERSEER: Get back inside!

1295
01:38:32.115 --> 01:38:33.480
(BOTH WHIMPERING)

1296
01:38:37.537 --> 01:38:40.029
Hurry. Get inside
the building.

1297
01:38:43.918 --> 01:38:45.249
(BOTH PANTING)

1298
01:38:50.133 --> 01:38:51.623
(THE BEAST PANTING)

1299
01:38:51.717 --> 01:38:53.879
ELIJAH: The water
used for David's room.

1300
01:38:53.970 --> 01:38:55.756
There's water in that tank.

1301
01:38:56.222 --> 01:38:58.429
I know he almost drowned
when he was a child.

1302
01:38:58.975 --> 01:39:00.886
Water is his weakness.

1303
01:39:02.687 --> 01:39:04.052
JOSEPH: Hey!

1304
01:39:04.147 --> 01:39:05.182
Hey!
OVERSEER: Joseph!

1305
01:39:05.273 --> 01:39:06.604
JOSEPH:
He's lying to you.

1306
01:39:06.691 --> 01:39:07.852
In comics.

1307
01:39:07.942 --> 01:39:11.526
the parents of the villains always
hold a key to understanding them.

1308
01:39:11.863 --> 01:39:13.524
He's not
telling you something.

1309
01:39:13.614 --> 01:39:15.104
OVERSEER: Joseph. get back.

1310
01:39:15.575 --> 01:39:17.031
(THE BEAST BREATHING HEAVILY)

1311
01:39:19.537 --> 01:39:21.869
Don't tell him yet.

1312
01:39:24.125 --> 01:39:27.538
Kevin's dad didn't just take
any train and not come home.

1313
01:39:28.254 --> 01:39:30.086
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1314
01:39:44.645 --> 01:39:47.512
TRAIN ANNOUNCER: <i>Eastrail 177.
Next stop. Philadelphia.</i>

1315
01:40:16.802 --> 01:40:19.169
JOSEPH: <i>He took the train
my dad was on.</i>

1316
01:40:19.263 --> 01:40:22.801
<i>The one that everyone died
except my dad.</i>

1317
01:40:29.899 --> 01:40:31.389
That's the key
to who you are.

1318
01:40:33.694 --> 01:40:36.527
Mr. Glass killed Kevin's dad.

1319
01:40:36.697 --> 01:40:38.062
(PANTING)

1320
01:40:38.991 --> 01:40:40.948
(GROWLING)

1321
01:40:42.161 --> 01:40:44.152
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1322
01:40:48.084 --> 01:40:49.620
(GROWLING)

1323
01:40:50.294 --> 01:40:52.251
ELIJAH: It's all evidence.
you see?

1324
01:40:52.630 --> 01:40:54.917
If that train crash
hadn't happened.

1325
01:40:55.091 --> 01:40:57.799
Kevin wouldn't have been
left alone with his mother.

1326
01:40:58.219 --> 01:41:00.551
If Kevin's mother wasn't allowed
to continue to abuse him.

1327
01:41:00.638 --> 01:41:03.471
then The Beast
wouldn't have had to be born.

1328
01:41:03.724 --> 01:41:06.261
What are the odds
that David Dunn

1329
01:41:06.435 --> 01:41:11.100
and Clarence Wendell Crumb
would be together that day?

1330
01:41:12.191 --> 01:41:13.773
Amazing.

1331
01:41:14.902 --> 01:41:18.941
I created you
as I created David.

1332
01:41:19.782 --> 01:41:22.399
It just took longer.

1333
01:41:23.286 --> 01:41:25.072
Nineteen years.

1334
01:41:25.705 --> 01:41:28.823
They almost convinced me
I was crazy.

1335
01:41:29.375 --> 01:41:33.585
I create superheroes.

1336
01:41:34.964 --> 01:41:38.548
I truly am a mastermind.

1337
01:41:40.511 --> 01:41:43.720
I thank you for what you did.

1338
01:41:45.141 --> 01:41:48.350
But I came to protect Kevin.

1339
01:41:50.563 --> 01:41:55.228
And I cannot trust you
to keep him safe.

1340
01:41:56.110 --> 01:41:57.726
(SCREAMING)
(SCREAMS)

1341
01:41:59.739 --> 01:42:00.979
OVERSEER: Hey.

1342
01:42:01.699 --> 01:42:03.815
We still haven't settled
that kneeling thing.

1343
01:42:03.951 --> 01:42:06.864
(LAUGHING) The classic turn.

1344
01:42:07.038 --> 01:42:09.530
The enemy becomes the ally

1345
01:42:09.707 --> 01:42:14.167
because of the hero's
unflinching sense of good.

1346
01:42:15.254 --> 01:42:16.710
(GRUNTS)
(ELIJAH GROANS)

1347
01:42:18.758 --> 01:42:21.216
(COUGHS. GROANS)

1348
01:42:21.302 --> 01:42:22.838
(THE BEAST GRUNTING)

1349
01:42:53.542 --> 01:42:55.408
(BONES CRACK)
(SCREAMING)

1350
01:43:33.582 --> 01:43:35.368
(COUGHING)

1351
01:43:41.632 --> 01:43:43.122
(CONTINUES COUGHING)

1352
01:43:45.344 --> 01:43:49.633
We will finish this
in front of the world.

1353
01:43:49.724 --> 01:43:51.465
(SIRENS WAILING)

1354
01:44:03.863 --> 01:44:05.343
(MRS. PRICE PANTING)
(ELIJAH GROANING)

1355
01:44:06.574 --> 01:44:08.656
Elijah.
(GASPING)

1356
01:44:08.743 --> 01:44:10.575
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

1357
01:44:19.211 --> 01:44:20.211
Release me.

1358
01:44:23.174 --> 01:44:24.664
(STRAINING)

1359
01:44:24.759 --> 01:44:27.251
Let me talk to
Kevin Wendell Crumb.

1360
01:44:27.344 --> 01:44:28.459
(STRAINING)

1361
01:44:28.554 --> 01:44:29.589
No!

1362
01:44:30.014 --> 01:44:31.800
(THE BEAST GRUNTING)

1363
01:44:34.769 --> 01:44:35.769
Release me.

1364
01:44:35.853 --> 01:44:38.470
I need to talk to
Kevin Wendell Crumb.

1365
01:44:39.106 --> 01:44:40.688
(CHOKING)

1366
01:44:41.275 --> 01:44:43.141
He needs me.

1367
01:44:43.944 --> 01:44:45.184
Kevin Wendell Crumb.

1368
01:44:47.406 --> 01:44:48.521
Kevin Wendell Crumb.

1369
01:44:49.241 --> 01:44:50.447
(YELLS)

1370
01:44:51.202 --> 01:44:53.034
Kevin Wendell Crumb.

1371
01:44:55.790 --> 01:44:57.201
(KEVIN PANTING)

1372
01:45:04.715 --> 01:45:05.796
(IN NORMAL TONE) Hey.

1373
01:45:06.634 --> 01:45:08.216
The Beast listened to me.

1374
01:45:09.386 --> 01:45:12.674
He couldn't do what he wanted.
You can tell him what to do.

1375
01:45:12.765 --> 01:45:14.347
I'm not in charge
of the light.

1376
01:45:14.433 --> 01:45:15.433
Yes!

1377
01:45:16.811 --> 01:45:18.222
Yes. you are.

1378
01:45:19.939 --> 01:45:21.725
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

1379
01:45:22.817 --> 01:45:24.433
It feels good.

1380
01:45:25.945 --> 01:45:27.026
Doesn't it?

1381
01:45:27.112 --> 01:45:28.273
Mmm-hmm.

1382
01:45:29.240 --> 01:45:33.108
Will you stay in the light
with me?

1383
01:45:33.494 --> 01:45:34.825
For a little while?

1384
01:45:47.132 --> 01:45:48.132
(SILENCED GUNSHOT)

1385
01:45:48.801 --> 01:45:50.383
(CHOKING)

1386
01:45:55.599 --> 01:45:56.805
(GRUNTS)

1387
01:45:59.186 --> 01:46:01.473
OFFICER: She was able
to turn him. Target down.

1388
01:46:18.205 --> 01:46:19.741
You guys gotta help him.

1389
01:46:19.832 --> 01:46:22.369
That's my dad.
He's trying to help you guys.

1390
01:46:22.459 --> 01:46:23.859
The guy in the green.
that's my dad.

1391
01:46:23.919 --> 01:46:26.206
He's trying to stop the Horde.
He's really weak.

1392
01:46:26.297 --> 01:46:27.628
(COUGHING)

1393
01:46:32.636 --> 01:46:34.468
(GRUNTING)

1394
01:46:44.273 --> 01:46:46.014
(MUFFLED SCREAMING)

1395
01:46:53.657 --> 01:46:55.398
(MUFFLED SCREAMING CONTINUES)

1396
01:47:04.501 --> 01:47:05.536
David.

1397
01:47:06.253 --> 01:47:09.120
David. take my hand.
Take it now!

1398
01:47:09.214 --> 01:47:10.955
(STRAINING)

1399
01:47:12.134 --> 01:47:13.750
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

1400
01:47:28.651 --> 01:47:29.937
(DOOR CLOSES)

1401
01:47:30.027 --> 01:47:31.313
(CHATTER STOPS)

1402
01:47:34.156 --> 01:47:35.442
It's just us.

1403
01:47:40.621 --> 01:47:42.828
DR. STAPLE: They sent me here
for you three.

1404
01:47:44.959 --> 01:47:46.449
Tell me the truth.

1405
01:47:47.336 --> 01:47:50.749
Did I almost convince you
you were an ordinary man?

1406
01:47:53.550 --> 01:47:55.507
I would have left you alone.

1407
01:47:56.345 --> 01:47:58.427
but when the Horde
showed up here.

1408
01:47:59.348 --> 01:48:01.555
then I just had to come.

1409
01:48:17.408 --> 01:48:19.408
MRS. PRICE: Didn't you tell me
there was a showdown

1410
01:48:19.451 --> 01:48:21.567
at the end of
a limited edition?

1411
01:48:21.662 --> 01:48:23.869
How come you didn't know
how it was gonna end?

1412
01:48:23.956 --> 01:48:25.196
No. Mama.

1413
01:48:25.749 --> 01:48:30.209
This is not a limited edition.

1414
01:48:31.088 --> 01:48:37.380
This was an origin story
(COUGHS) the whole time.

1415
01:48:57.448 --> 01:48:58.529
(GROANS)

1416
01:49:00.826 --> 01:49:02.533
What's happening?

1417
01:49:02.619 --> 01:49:03.859
(GRUNTS)

1418
01:49:05.289 --> 01:49:06.529
(CRYING)

1419
01:49:07.458 --> 01:49:09.574
(AS HEDWIG) I like being nine.

1420
01:49:10.753 --> 01:49:12.164
(SNIFFLING)

1421
01:49:12.254 --> 01:49:15.667
It hurts. Casey.
Get it to stop hurting.

1422
01:49:16.050 --> 01:49:17.381
(CHOKING)

1423
01:49:17.468 --> 01:49:21.177
I can't hold on
to the light. Casey.

1424
01:49:22.181 --> 01:49:23.842
(STRAINED GRUNTING)
(CRYING)

1425
01:49:25.559 --> 01:49:29.268
(AS DENNIS) I should never
have listened to her.

1426
01:49:29.605 --> 01:49:31.095
(PAINED GRUNTING)

1427
01:49:33.609 --> 01:49:37.227
Now these pants got blood
on them. They're ruined.

1428
01:49:37.488 --> 01:49:39.399
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

1429
01:49:39.490 --> 01:49:42.323
We gotta clean these pants.
Casey.

1430
01:49:42.534 --> 01:49:44.024
(CHOKING)

1431
01:49:44.745 --> 01:49:46.782
(AS SAMUEL)
As his body slowly succumbs

1432
01:49:46.872 --> 01:49:48.362
to the inevitable.

1433
01:49:48.749 --> 01:49:53.494
a sensation of cold water
spreads through his body.

1434
01:49:54.171 --> 01:49:57.289
His thoughts are
a mixture of fear

1435
01:49:57.466 --> 01:50:00.208
and sweet relief.

1436
01:50:00.928 --> 01:50:02.293
(STRAINING)

1437
01:50:02.930 --> 01:50:03.990
(AS POLLY)
Ladies and gentlemen.

1438
01:50:04.014 --> 01:50:05.470
here's Patricia.

1439
01:50:05.557 --> 01:50:07.924
We should all listen to her.

1440
01:50:08.519 --> 01:50:09.805
(STRAINS)

1441
01:50:09.895 --> 01:50:11.431
(AS PATRICIA)
Did you see them?

1442
01:50:12.106 --> 01:50:15.098
They are both extraordinary.

1443
01:50:15.275 --> 01:50:16.936
I never doubted...

1444
01:50:17.945 --> 01:50:22.064
Never let them tell you
I doubted it.

1445
01:50:23.742 --> 01:50:25.358
(GASPING)

1446
01:50:25.536 --> 01:50:27.243
(IN NORMAL TONE)
They're all so scared.

1447
01:50:29.164 --> 01:50:31.781
But I told them that I'm gonna
hold the light now.

1448
01:50:35.212 --> 01:50:37.294
You really my friend?

1449
01:50:39.967 --> 01:50:42.254
Then I'm gonna
hold the light till the end.

1450
01:50:42.845 --> 01:50:44.631
Till the very end.

1451
01:50:47.516 --> 01:50:49.928
It's not so bad
being in the light.

1452
01:50:51.728 --> 01:50:53.014
(GASPING)

1453
01:50:59.486 --> 01:51:00.567
(SOFTLY) Kevin.

1454
01:51:07.035 --> 01:51:08.525
(INAUDIBLE)

1455
01:51:38.483 --> 01:51:41.692
DR. STAPLE: Would you mind stepping
away for a moment so I can check him?

1456
01:51:44.907 --> 01:51:46.318
It's okay.

1457
01:51:53.665 --> 01:51:54.951
(ELIJAH COUGHS)

1458
01:51:56.752 --> 01:51:57.958
(ELIJAH GASPS)

1459
01:52:05.260 --> 01:52:07.046
They got it wrong
in the comics.

1460
01:52:09.014 --> 01:52:13.383
They talk about secret evil
groups trying to stop the heroes.

1461
01:52:13.560 --> 01:52:15.972
I don't think we are
particularly evil

1462
01:52:16.146 --> 01:52:18.103
and we don't choose sides.

1463
01:52:18.982 --> 01:52:20.814
We try to stop both of you.

1464
01:52:21.985 --> 01:52:23.601
If there is one of you.

1465
01:52:24.238 --> 01:52:28.323
the opposite of you appears.
It escalates. We step in.

1466
01:52:29.201 --> 01:52:32.410
There just can't be gods
amongst us.

1467
01:52:33.538 --> 01:52:34.869
It's not fair.

1468
01:52:35.666 --> 01:52:40.160
It has worked just fine
for 10.000 years our way.

1469
01:52:41.129 --> 01:52:44.918
Take consolation in the fact that
you were right about your theory.

1470
01:52:47.511 --> 01:52:49.172
Be at peace.

1471
01:53:08.115 --> 01:53:13.326
I wasn't a mistake. Mama.

1472
01:53:14.579 --> 01:53:15.694
MRS. PRICE: No.

1473
01:53:17.833 --> 01:53:20.450
You were spectacular.

1474
01:53:20.585 --> 01:53:21.791
Oh.

1475
01:53:32.431 --> 01:53:33.842
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

1476
01:53:37.728 --> 01:53:40.345
DR. STAPLE: <i>These patients
were very disturbed.</i>

1477
01:53:41.023 --> 01:53:42.855
<i>Let me just simply state.</i>

1478
01:53:42.941 --> 01:53:45.649
<i>everything that occurred was
related to drugs in their systems</i>

1479
01:53:45.736 --> 01:53:48.398
<i>or their heightened
state of mania.</i>

1480
01:53:48.488 --> 01:53:49.694
<i>For the patients' privacy.</i>

1481
01:53:49.781 --> 01:53:53.900
let's keep what happened in this building
and this parking lot to ourselves.

1482
01:53:55.620 --> 01:53:56.764
REPORTER:
<i>...general public alike.</i>

1483
01:53:56.788 --> 01:53:58.199
<i>Opening ceremonies
have concluded.</i>

1484
01:53:58.290 --> 01:54:00.657
<i>but from the looks on the
faces of the thousands...</i>

1485
01:54:07.215 --> 01:54:08.671
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

1486
01:54:23.190 --> 01:54:24.726
(DOOR CLOSES)

1487
01:54:25.984 --> 01:54:27.440
(CHATTER STOPS)

1488
01:54:37.204 --> 01:54:38.990
DR. STAPLE:
All three were real.

1489
01:54:41.083 --> 01:54:43.120
Quite special. actually.

1490
01:54:45.170 --> 01:54:48.834
If you approve.
I will move to the next city.

1491
01:54:49.925 --> 01:54:51.916
WOMAN: Will there be
any repercussions?

1492
01:54:52.427 --> 01:54:53.963
DR. STAPLE:
No one saw them.

1493
01:54:55.013 --> 01:54:57.220
I know what my charge is.

1494
01:54:58.266 --> 01:54:59.882
Convince them.

1495
01:55:00.060 --> 01:55:03.394
This is the most humane
and effective method.

1496
01:55:03.980 --> 01:55:07.439
We're not executioners.
and we don't need martyrs.

1497
01:55:07.943 --> 01:55:10.810
If that fails.
use the machine.

1498
01:55:11.613 --> 01:55:15.151
And I understand how important
what we're doing is.

1499
01:55:16.076 --> 01:55:17.908
Maintaining balance.

1500
01:55:18.787 --> 01:55:20.198
keeping order.

1501
01:55:42.185 --> 01:55:44.705
BATMAN: (ON TV) <i>We're not here
to buy umbrellas and you know it.</i>

1502
01:55:44.855 --> 01:55:47.017
ROBIN: <i>Spread your wings.
Mr. K. G. Bird.</i>

1503
01:55:47.107 --> 01:55:48.814
<i>We're flying you down
to headquarters.</i>

1504
01:55:49.276 --> 01:55:51.859
THE PENGUIN:
<i>On what charge. Boy Wonder?</i>

1505
01:55:52.028 --> 01:55:53.063
ROBIN: <i>Illegal umbrellas.</i>

1506
01:55:53.238 --> 01:55:55.275
BATMAN: <i>Assault and battery.
disturbing the peace.</i>

1507
01:55:55.449 --> 01:55:58.237
<i>We've got enough to put
you back on ice. Penguin.</i>

1508
01:55:58.452 --> 01:56:00.159
(UPBEAT ROCK SONG PLAYING
ON SPEAKERS)

1509
01:56:06.668 --> 01:56:07.908
He's too smart.

1510
01:56:08.253 --> 01:56:10.164
That's why
he's the mastermind.

1511
01:56:10.714 --> 01:56:12.876
He'll never tell you
his real plan.

1512
01:56:13.300 --> 01:56:16.167
He sets everybody up.
Gets them looking in one direction.

1513
01:56:17.345 --> 01:56:18.631
BOY: So cool. man.

1514
01:56:19.306 --> 01:56:21.889
There's always
a real plan.

1515
01:56:32.319 --> 01:56:33.855
You see this camera?

1516
01:56:34.905 --> 01:56:37.112
There are 100 more
of these.

1517
01:56:37.699 --> 01:56:41.067
Everything is being recorded.

1518
01:56:49.669 --> 01:56:52.752
<i>All videos and all back-up
videos have been erased. correct?</i>

1519
01:56:52.839 --> 01:56:53.839
GUARD: <i>Yes.</i>

1520
01:56:54.549 --> 01:56:56.631
Was any of it downloaded
before that?

1521
01:56:59.346 --> 01:57:00.836
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

1522
01:57:05.602 --> 01:57:07.889
GUARD: I don't know
how this is possible.

1523
01:57:08.063 --> 01:57:12.682
Someone was streaming the live
security feed to a private site.

1524
01:57:17.739 --> 01:57:19.195
(KEYBOARD CLACKING)

1525
01:57:37.884 --> 01:57:40.296
He went through the
basement tunnels to be seen

1526
01:57:40.387 --> 01:57:42.594
by as many cameras
as possible.

1527
01:57:42.681 --> 01:57:45.298
That's why he didn't go out
the side entrance.

1528
01:57:46.810 --> 01:57:49.472
<i>He was never planning
on going to that building.</i>

1529
01:57:52.315 --> 01:57:54.773
This was a suicide mission.

1530
01:57:56.236 --> 01:57:59.854
I gave him all the cameras
he needed right here.

1531
01:58:11.626 --> 01:58:14.493
What have you done. Elijah?

1532
01:58:16.798 --> 01:58:18.129
(DOOR OPENS)

1533
01:58:19.301 --> 01:58:20.507
(DOOR CLOSES)

1534
01:58:28.184 --> 01:58:30.141
(SCREAMING)

1535
01:58:35.817 --> 01:58:36.852
(SIGHS)

1536
01:58:36.943 --> 01:58:38.479
(KIDS PLAYING OUTSIDE)

1537
01:58:43.408 --> 01:58:45.069
(COMPUTER CHIMES)

1538
01:59:01.009 --> 01:59:02.215
(SIGHS)

1539
01:59:07.390 --> 01:59:08.630
(MOUSE CLICKS)

1540
01:59:11.019 --> 01:59:12.622
ELIJAH: (ON SPEAKERS)
<i>There are unknown forces</i>

1541
01:59:12.646 --> 01:59:16.435
<i>that don't want us to realize
what we are truly capable of.</i>

1542
01:59:19.277 --> 01:59:20.608
<i>They don't want us to know</i>

1543
01:59:20.695 --> 01:59:25.064
<i>the things we suspect are
extraordinary about ourselves are real.</i>

1544
01:59:26.076 --> 01:59:27.487
(COMPUTER CHIMES)

1545
01:59:37.003 --> 01:59:39.085
<i>I believe
that if everyone sees</i>

1546
01:59:39.422 --> 01:59:44.007
<i>what just a few people become when
they wholly embrace their gifts.</i>

1547
01:59:44.511 --> 01:59:46.843
<i>others will awaken.</i>

1548
01:59:50.558 --> 01:59:55.348
<i>Belief in oneself
is contagious.</i>

1549
01:59:56.314 --> 02:00:00.308
<i>We give each other permission
to be superheroes.</i>

1550
02:00:01.027 --> 02:00:04.645
<i>We will never
awaken otherwise.</i>

1551
02:00:04.739 --> 02:00:06.821
(KIDS CHATTERING)

1552
02:00:11.246 --> 02:00:13.533
<i>Whoever these people are</i>

1553
02:00:13.707 --> 02:00:16.790
<i>who don't want us
to know the truth.</i>

1554
02:00:17.794 --> 02:00:20.957
<i>today they lose.</i>

1555
02:00:36.646 --> 02:00:38.102
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

1556
02:00:47.532 --> 02:00:48.647
Thanks.

1557
02:00:57.542 --> 02:01:00.034
How long's it been
since we posted it?

1558
02:01:01.087 --> 02:01:02.373
Two hours.

1559
02:01:07.969 --> 02:01:09.380
How long
will it be before...

1560
02:01:09.471 --> 02:01:10.836
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENT
ON PA)

1561
02:01:13.183 --> 02:01:14.673
(INAUDIBLE CONVERSATIONS)

1562
02:01:29.199 --> 02:01:30.860
(SIGHS. SNIFFLES)

1563
02:01:41.544 --> 02:01:42.544
(EXHALES)

1564
02:02:03.149 --> 02:02:04.935
I know what this is.

1565
02:02:08.822 --> 02:02:12.406
This is the moment we are
let in on the universe.

1566
02:02:51.698 --> 02:02:53.484
(INAUDIBLE)

1566
